---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import '../styles/global.css';
---
<BaseLayout>
  <div class="cursor" aria-hidden="true"><span></span></div>

  <header class="masthead" data-masthead>
    <a class="wordmark" href="#top" aria-label="Boomley home">BOOMLEY®</a>
    <p class="masthead-note">Two people building around problems worth solving.</p>
    <a class="masthead-action" href="#signal-box">Send a signal ↗</a>
  </header>

  <main id="top">
    <section class="cover act act--paper" aria-labelledby="cover-title">
      <div class="cover-copy">
        <p class="edition" data-reveal>ISSUE 001 / A COMPANY IN THE MAKING</p>
        <h1 id="cover-title" class="cover-title" data-cover-title>
          BUILD THE THINGS<br />
          PEOPLE <em>WISH</em><br />
          EXISTED.
        </h1>
        <p class="cover-deck" data-reveal>
          Boomley listens for the things people keep putting up with — then builds when the signal is strong enough.
        </p>
        <div class="cover-foot" data-reveal>
          <span>PRODUCT × ENGINEERING</span>
          <span>CURRENTLY / PRODUCT 001</span>
          <span>STATUS / STILL BECOMING</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="cover-portrait cover-portrait--a" data-reveal>
        <div class="sprite founder-shot sprite-chidi" role="img" aria-label="Chidi, Product"></div>
        <span>01 / PRODUCT</span>
      </div>
      <div class="cover-portrait cover-portrait--b" data-reveal>
        <div class="sprite founder-shot sprite-michael" role="img" aria-label="Michael, Engineering"></div>
        <span>02 / ENGINEERING</span>
      </div>

      <div class="cover-mark cover-mark--blue">THERE HAS TO BE A BETTER WAY.</div>
      <div class="cover-mark cover-mark--ink">2 PEOPLE / 1 PRODUCT / BOX OPEN</div>
      <div class="blue-envelope blue-envelope--cover" aria-hidden="true" data-travelling-envelope>
        <span>TO / BOOMLEY</span>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="noise act act--ink" id="signal-story">
      <div class="noise-stage" data-noise-stage>
        <p class="chapter">01 / WHAT WE NOTICE</p>

        <div class="noise-fragment noise-fragment--1">Why does this still take six steps?</div>
        <div class="noise-fragment noise-fragment--2">I need three apps just to do one thing.</div>
        <div class="noise-fragment noise-fragment--3">Surely this can be simpler.</div>
        <div class="noise-fragment noise-fragment--4">Why have we accepted this?</div>
        <div class="noise-fragment noise-fragment--5">There has to be a better way.</div>
        <div class="noise-fragment noise-fragment--6">I wish something existed that...</div>

        <div class="noise-ascii" aria-hidden="true" data-noise-ascii>
....:::;;;;iiirrssXXAA253hMHHGSS##9B&@
..:::;;;iiirrssXXAA253hMHHGSS##9B&@@
.::;;;iiirrssXXAA253hMHHGSS##9B&@@@
::;;;iiirrssXXAA253hMHHGSS##9B&@@@@
        </div>

        <div class="signal-resolve" data-signal-resolve>
          <span class="chapter">THE MOMENT IT REPEATS</span>
          <h2>THAT'S<br /><em>A SIGNAL.</em></h2>
          <p>Not an app idea. Not a pitch. A repeated pain point with enough weight to deserve attention.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="people act act--paper" id="founders">
      <div class="people-intro">
        <p class="chapter">02 / THE PEOPLE OPENING THE BOX</p>
        <h2 class="serif-heading" data-reveal>Product asks <em>why.</em><br />Engineering asks <em>how.</em></h2>
        <p class="people-intro-copy" data-reveal>Boomley lives somewhere between those two questions.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="people-composition">
        <article class="person person--primary" tabindex="0" data-person>
          <div class="person-media">
            <div class="sprite person-photo sprite-chidi" role="img" aria-label="Chidi portrait"></div>
            <div class="sprite person-ascii sprite-chidi-ascii" role="img" aria-label="ASCII interpretation of Chidi portrait"></div>
            <div class="person-hover">
              <span>BOOMLEY / 01</span>
              <strong>PRODUCT</strong>
              <small>X / HANDLE TO ADD</small>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="person-caption">
            <span>01</span>
            <h3>CHIDI</h3>
            <p>Product management / research / experience / strategy</p>
          </div>
        </article>

        <article class="person person--secondary" tabindex="0" data-person>
          <div class="person-media">
            <div class="sprite person-photo sprite-michael" role="img" aria-label="Michael portrait"></div>
            <div class="sprite person-ascii sprite-michael-ascii" role="img" aria-label="ASCII interpretation of Michael portrait"></div>
            <div class="person-hover">
              <span>BOOMLEY / 02</span>
              <strong>ENGINEERING</strong>
              <small>X / HANDLE TO ADD</small>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="person-caption">
            <span>02</span>
            <h3>MICHAEL</h3>
            <p>Software engineering / systems / architecture / build</p>
          </div>
        </article>

        <p class="people-side-note">TWO PEOPLE.<br />FOR NOW.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="product act act--paper" id="product">
      <div class="product-prologue">
        <p class="chapter">03 / PRODUCT 001</p>
        <p class="product-prologue-line" data-reveal>WE NOTICED SOMETHING.</p>
        <p class="product-prologue-line product-prologue-line--serif" data-reveal>So we kept pulling at it.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="product-documentary">
        <div class="product-document product-document--research" data-doc>
          <span>RESEARCH / 001</span>
          <h3>Attention was fragmented long before we tried to fix it.</h3>
          <p>Tasks here. Notes there. Timers somewhere else. Study tools in another tab. The tools were becoming part of the problem.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="product-document product-document--system" data-doc>
          <span>SYSTEM / 001</span>
          <div class="system-sketch" aria-hidden="true">
            <i>INTENT</i><b>→</b><i>FOCUS</i><b>→</b><i>COMMIT</i><b>→</b><i>FINISH</i>
          </div>
          <p>We started designing around intention instead of adding another list of features.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="product-reveal" data-product-reveal>
          <span class="chapter">PRIVATE BUILD / SIGNAL 001</span>
          <h2>DECLUTTER.</h2>
          <p>A calmer environment for serious learners and builders who want their attention to mean something.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="build-thread" data-build-thread>
        <div class="thread-line" aria-hidden="true"></div>
        <article class="done"><span>01</span><h3>RESEARCH</h3><small>COMPLETE</small></article>
        <article class="done"><span>02</span><h3>DOCUMENTATION</h3><small>COMPLETE</small></article>
        <article class="active"><span>03</span><h3>EXPERIENCE</h3><small>YOU ARE HERE</small></article>
        <article><span>04</span><h3>BUILD</h3><small>NEXT</small></article>
        <article><span>05</span><h3>TEST</h3><small>QUEUED</small></article>
        <article><span>06</span><h3>RELEASE</h3><small>WHEN READY</small></article>
      </div>

      <div class="early-access" data-reveal>
        <div>
          <span class="chapter">EARLY ACCESS</span>
          <h3>THIS ISN'T<br />FOR EVERYONE.</h3>
          <p>Good. Declutter is being built for people willing to take their own intentions seriously.</p>
        </div>
        <form class="waitlist-form" name="declutter-waitlist" method="POST" data-netlify="true" netlify-honeypot="bot-field" data-netlify-form>
          <input type="hidden" name="form-name" value="declutter-waitlist" />
          <p class="honeypot"><label>Do not fill this out: <input name="bot-field" /></label></p>
          <label for="waitlist-email">Coming soon — be among the first to experience real lock-in power.</label>
          <div class="email-line">
            <input id="waitlist-email" type="email" name="email" placeholder="ENTER EMAIL" autocomplete="email" required />
            <button type="submit">I'M SERIOUS ↗</button>
          </div>
          <p class="form-status" data-form-status aria-live="polite"></p>
        </form>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="signal-box act act--mist" id="signal-box">
      <div class="signal-box-intro">
        <p class="chapter">04 / THE BOX IS OPEN</p>
        <h2 class="serif-heading" data-reveal>Product 001 came from <em>a signal.</em><br />Product 002 might come from yours.</h2>
        <div class="signal-box-instructions" data-reveal>
          <strong>WRITE THE PROBLEM.</strong>
          <strong>WRAP THE LETTER.</strong>
          <strong>POST IT.</strong>
          <p>Don't pitch us an app. Tell us what should not still be this difficult.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="signal-box-workspace" data-signal-stage>
        <form class="letter" name="boomley-signal" method="POST" data-netlify="true" netlify-honeypot="bot-field" data-signal-form>
          <input type="hidden" name="form-name" value="boomley-signal" />
          <p class="honeypot"><label>Do not fill this out: <input name="bot-field" /></label></p>

          <div class="letter-meta">
            <span>BOOMLEY / SIGNAL FORM</span>
            <span>001</span>
          </div>
          <h3>WHAT HAVE YOU NOTICED?</h3>
          <p class="letter-note">Write the problem. We'll worry about the product.</p>

          <label>THE PROBLEM
            <textarea name="friction" rows="4" required placeholder="It shouldn't still be this difficult to..."></textarea>
          </label>
          <label>WHO DEALS WITH IT?
            <input name="who" type="text" required placeholder="People who..." />
          </label>
          <label>WHAT CHANGES IF IT'S FIXED?
            <textarea name="change" rows="2" required placeholder="It would make it easier to..."></textarea>
          </label>
          <label>YOUR EMAIL
            <input name="email" type="email" required autocomplete="email" placeholder="you@example.com" />
          </label>

          <div class="letter-actions">
            <button type="button" class="action action--blue" data-wrap-button>WRAP IT →</button>
            <button type="submit" class="action action--red" data-post-button disabled>POST IT →</button>
          </div>
          <p class="form-status" data-signal-status aria-live="polite"></p>
        </form>

        <div class="posting-stage">
          <div class="blue-envelope blue-envelope--signal" data-blue-envelope aria-hidden="true">
            <div class="envelope-paper">SIGNAL / READY</div>
            <div class="envelope-flap"></div>
            <span>TO / BOOMLEY</span>
          </div>

          <div class="pillar-shell" data-pillar-box aria-label="Boomley Signal Box">
            <div class="pillar-top"></div>
            <div class="pillar-cylinder">
              <div class="pillar-slot"><span>POST SIGNAL</span></div>
              <div class="pillar-plaque"><b>BOOMLEY</b><small>SIGNAL RECEIVER / 001</small></div>
              <div class="pillar-door"><span>THE BOX IS OPEN</span></div>
            </div>
            <div class="pillar-foot"></div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="continuation act act--ink">
      <div class="continuation-ascii" aria-hidden="true">
SIGNAL / SIGNAL / SIGNAL / SIGNAL / SIGNAL
00100010 01110101 01101001 01101100 01100100
PEOPLE × PROBLEMS × PRODUCTS
THE BOX IS OPEN
      </div>
      <div class="continuation-copy">
        <span class="chapter">TO BE CONTINUED</span>
        <h2 class="serif-heading" data-reveal>001 is just<br /><em>the first one.</em></h2>
        <p data-reveal>There are more signals out there. We're listening.</p>
      </div>
      <footer class="footer">
        <span>BOOMLEY® © 2026</span>
        <span>PRODUCT × ENGINEERING</span>
        <a href="#signal-box">SEND SOMETHING ↑</a>
      </footer>
    </section>
  </main>

  <script>
    import '../scripts/home.ts';
  </script>
</BaseLayout>
